:[{"href":"http:\/\/walkpono.org\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/media?parent=75"}],"curies":[{"name":"wp","href":"https:\/\/api.w.org\/{rel}","templated":true}]}},{"id":36,"date":"2019-06-23T05:36:56","date_gmt":"2019-06-23T05:36:56","guid":{"rendered":"http:\/\/walkpono.org\/?page_id=36"},"modified":"2020-04-13T08:09:01","modified_gmt":"2020-04-13T08:09:01","slug":"about-us","status":"publish","type":"page","link":"http:\/\/walkpono.org\/about-us\/","title":{"rendered":"ABOUT US"},"content":{"rendered":"<h2><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" class=\"size-medium wp-image-37 alignleft\" src=\"http:\/\/walkpono.org\/wp-content\/uploads\/2019\/06\/1914610_545503195510_2748970_n-225x300.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"225\" height=\"300\" srcset=\"http:\/\/walkpono.org\/wp-content\/uploads\/2019\/06\/1914610_545503195510_2748970_n-225x300.jpg 225w, http:\/\/walkpono.org\/wp-content\/uploads\/2019\/06\/1914610_545503195510_2748970_n.jpg 540w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 225px) 100vw, 225px\" \/><strong>Aaron-Michael Ho<\/strong><\/h2>\n<p>Greatness Guru &amp; Transformational Linguist, Aaron-Michael Ho is the founder and operator of WalkPono LLC: The Greatness Institute. Working with groups, as well as individuals, WalkPono seeks to deepen understanding of the concepts <em>aloha <\/em>and <em>pono<\/em>; to encourage wholeness and healing in Hawai\u02bbi and beyond! A long-time Hawaiian language teacher, a cultural body work practitioner and formerly of the Cultural Resources team at Bishop Museum (the Hawai\u02bbi State Museum of Cultural and Natural History), Aaron found a calling in combining his love and adoration for his native culture with his passion for coaching and creating space for healing!<\/p>\n<div><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" class=\"size-medium wp-image-187 alignright\" src=\"http:\/\/walkpono.org\/wp-content\/uploads\/2019\/12\/IMG_0069-169x300.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"169\" height=\"300\" srcset=\"http:\/\/walkpono.org\/wp-content\/uploads\/2019\/12\/IMG_0069-169x300.png 169w, http:\/\/walkpono.org\/wp-content\/uploads\/2019\/12\/IMG_0069-576x1024.png 576w, http:\/\/walkpono.org\/wp-content\/uploads\/2019\/12\/IMG_0069-768x1365.png 768w, http:\/\/walkpono.org\/wp-content\/uploads\/2019\/12\/IMG_0069-864x1536.png 864w, http:\/\/walkpono.org\/wp-content\/uploads\/2019\/12\/IMG_0069-1152x2048.png 1152w, http:\/\/walkpono.org\/wp-content\/uploads\/2019\/12\/IMG_0069.png 1242w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 169px) 100vw, 169px\" \/><\/div>\n<p><a id=\"services\"><\/p>\n<div>From keynote speaking to classroom teaching, or from one-on-one coaching to large-scale workshop facilitation, Aaron crafts masterfully interactive experiences ensuring each student or attendee comes away with a deeper, richer understanding of the topic engaged.<\/div>\n<p><\/a><\/p>\n<div><\/div>\n<div>WalkPono LLC considers itself very blessed to have had the opportunity to partner with such organizations as Hawai\u02bbi Maoli, Hawaii Community Assets, AmeriCorps VISTAs, the American Red Cross, CoachKaipo.com, and the Mindful Forgiveness Center&#8230;just to name a few.<\/div>\n<div><\/div>\n<p>&nbsp;<\/p>\n<div><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" class=\"alignleft size-medium wp-image-182\" src=\"http:\/\/walkpono.org\/wp-content\/uploads\/2019\/12\/IMG_0071-1-300x169.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"300\" height=\"169\" srcset=\"http:\/\/walkpono.org\/wp-content\/uploads\/2019\/12\/IMG_0071-1-300x169.png 300w, http:\/\/walkpono.org\/wp-content\/uploads\/2019\/12\/IMG_0071-1-1024x576.png 1024w, http:\/\/walkpono.org\/wp-content\/uploads\/2019\/12\/IMG_0071-1-768x432.png 768w, http:\/\/walkpono.org\/wp-content\/uploads\/2019\/12\/IMG_0071-1.png 1150w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 300px) 100vw, 300px\" \/><\/div>\n<div>The name of the game is &#8220;experiential learning.&#8221; \u00a0WalkPono LLC: The Greatness Institute offers a myriad of classes and workshops, and none of them are about textbook teaching and lecture. \u00a0We play games, engage in activities, hold discussions and debates&#8230;the content comes alive.<\/div>\n<blockquote>\n<div>After all, studied content might be fleeting&#8230;but you\u02bbll remember your experiences for a lifetime!<\/div>\n<\/blockquote>\n<div><\/div>\n<hr \/>\n<div><\/div>\n","protected":false},"excerpt":{"rendered":"<p>Aaron-Michael Ho Greatness Guru &amp; Transformational Linguist, Aaron-Michael Ho is the founder and operator of WalkPono LLC: The Greatness Institute. Working with groups, as well as individuals, WalkPono seeks to deepen understanding of the concepts aloha and pono; to encourage wholeness and healing in Hawai\u02bbi and beyond! A long-time Hawaiian language teacher, a cultural body &hellip; <\/p>\n<p class=\"link-more\"><a href=\"http:\/\/walkpono.org\/about-us\/\" class=\"more-link\">Continue reading<span class=\"screen-reader-text\"> &#8220;ABOUT US&#8221;<\/span><\/a><\/p>\n","protected":false},"author":1,"featured_media":0,"parent":0,"menu_order":0,"comment_status":"closed","ping_status":"closed","template":"","meta":{"spay_email":""},"_links":{"self":[{"href":"http:\/\/walkpono.org\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/pages\/36"}],"collection":[{"href":"http:\/\/walkpono.org\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/pages"}],"about":[{"href":"http:\/\/walkpono.org\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/types\/page"}],"author":[{"embeddable":true,"href":"http:\/\/walkpono.org\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/users\/1"}],"replies":[{"embeddable":true,"href":"http:\/\/walkpono.org\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/comments?post=36"}],"version-history":[{"count":15,"href":"http:\/\/walkpono.org\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/pages\/36\/revisions"}],"predecessor-version":[{"id":317,"href":"http:\/\/walkpono.org\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/pages\/36\/revisions\/317"}],"wp:attachment":[{"href":"http:\/\/walkpono.org\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/media?parent=36"}],"curies":[{"name":"wp","href":"https:\/\/api.w.org\/{rel}","templated":true}]}},{"id":40,"date":"2019-06-13T19:24:01","date_gmt":"2019-06-13T19:24:01","guid":{"rendered":"http:\/\/walkpono.org\/?page_id=40"},"modified":"2023-05-29T05:53:17","modified_gmt":"2023-05-29T05:53:17","slug":"1-on-1-or-group-coaching","status":"publish","type":"page","link":"http:\/\/walkpono.org\/1-on-1-or-group-coaching\/","title":{"rendered":"1-on-1 or Group Coaching"},"content":{"rendered":"<h1>1-on-1 or Group Coaching<\/h1>\n<p>&#8220;Never Surf Alone! Never Lift Alone! Also&#8230; Never Life Alone! Find Yourself a Workout Partner!&#8221; &#8211; The Greatness Guru<\/p>\n<p>In the beautiful surroundings of Hawai\u02bbi, we are instilled with important wisdom from an early age: 1) Never turn your back on the ocean, and 2) Never surf alone. When out in the water, having a companion becomes invaluable. They provide an extra set of eyes, whether it&#8217;s observing the incoming sets or monitoring the changing tides. They can also lend a helping hand by blocking for you or alerting you when you&#8217;re on someone else&#8217;s wave. And in the unfortunate event of an accident, having someone who knows what happened can make all the difference.<\/p>\n<p>But this principle of &#8220;never&#8230; alone&#8221; extends far beyond surfing. In the weight room, it&#8217;s &#8220;never lift alone!&#8221; On the trails, it&#8217;s &#8220;never hike alone!&#8221; And whether on the roads or rails, it&#8217;s &#8220;never travel alone!&#8221; With countless activities and experiences in life, why would you ever choose to go through it alone?<\/p>\n<p>Here at WalkPono LLC: The Greatness Institute, we offer our skills and professional expertise to accompany you on your journey through life. Through years of study and practice, we have identified the areas where the mind and spirit often face challenges. Armed with our arsenal of tools, some tried and true, others developed specifically for our approach, we are here to join forces with you. Together, we will help you refine your skills, strategize your game plan, and elevate your expertise to new heights in your chosen field.<\/p>\n<p>Let us embark on this journey together, and through our collaboration, unleash your true greatness.<\/p>\n","protected":false},"excerpt":{"rendered":"<p>1-on-1 or Group Coaching &#8220;Never Surf Alone! Never Lift Alone! Also&#8230; Never Life Alone! Find Yourself a Workout Partner!&#8221; &#8211; The Greatness Guru In the beautiful surroundings of Hawai\u02bbi, we are instilled with important wisdom from an early age: 1) Never turn your back on the ocean, and 2) Never surf alone. When out in &hellip; <\/p>\n<p class=\"link-more\"><a href=\"http:\/\/walkpono.org\/1-on-1-or-group-coaching\/\" class=\"more-link\">Continue reading<span class=\"screen-reader-text\"> &#8220;1-on-1 or Group Coaching&#8221;<\/span><\/a><\/p>\n","protected":false},"author":1,"featured_media":41,"parent":0,"menu_order":0,"comment_status":"closed","ping_status":"closed","template":"","meta":{"spay_email":""},"_links":{"self":[{"href":"http:\/\/walkpono.org\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/pages\/40"}],"collection":[{"href":"http:\/\/walkpono.org\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/pages"}],"about":[{"href":"http:\/\/walkpono.org\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/types\/page"}],"author":[{"embeddable":true,"href":"http:\/\/walkpono.org\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/users\/1"}],"replies":[{"embeddable":true,"href":"http:\/\/walkpono.org\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/comments?post=40"}],"version-history":[{"count":7,"href":"http:\/\/walkpono.org\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/pages\/40\/revisions"}],"predecessor-version":[{"id":354,"href":"http:\/\/walkpono.org\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/pages\/40\/revisions\/354"}],"wp:featuredmedia":[{"embeddable":true,"href":"http:\/\/walkpono.org\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/media\/41"}],"wp:attachment":[{"href":"http:\/\/walkpono.org\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/media?parent=40"}],"curies":[{"name":"wp","href":"https:\/\/api.w.org\/{rel}","templated":true}]}},{"id":23,"date":"2019-06-02T04:36:03","date_gmt":"2019-06-02T04:36:03","guid":{"rendered":"http:\/\/walkpono.org\/?page_id=23"},"modified":"2020-10-28T07:22:06","modified_gmt":"2020-10-28T07:22:06","slug":"blog","status":"publish","type":"page","link":"http:\/\/walkpono.org\/blog\/","title":{"rendered":"ARTICLES"},"content":{"rendered":"","protected":false},"excerpt":{"rendered":"","protected":false},"author":1,"featured_media":0,"parent":0,"menu_order":0,"comment_status":"closed","ping_status":"closed","template":"","meta":{"spay_email":""},"_links":{"self":[{"href":"http:\/\/walkpono.org\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/pages\/23"}],"collection":[{"href":"http:\/\/walkpono.org\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/pages"}],"about":[{"href":"http:\/\/walkpono.org\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/types\/page"}],"author":[{"embeddable":true,"href":"http:\/\/walkpono.org\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/users\/1"}],"replies":[{"embeddable":true,"href":"http:\/\/walkpono.org\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/comments?post=23"}],"version-history":[{"count":2,"href":"http:\/\/walkpono.org\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/pages\/23\/revisions"}],"predecessor-version":[{"id":29,"href":"http:\/\/walkpono.org\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/pages\/23\/revisions\/29"}],"wp:attachment":[{"href":"http:\/\/walkpono.org\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/media?parent=23"}],"curies":[{"name":"wp","href":"https:\/\/api.w.org\/{rel}","templated":true}]}},{"id":15,"date":"2019-06-02T04:21:52","date_gmt":"2019-06-02T04:21:52","guid":{"rendered":"http:\/\/walkpono.org\/?page_id=15"},"modified":"2023-05-29T05:38:01","modified_gmt":"2023-05-29T05:38:01","slug":"under-construction","status":"publish","type":"page","link":"http:\/\/walkpono.org\/","title":{"rendered":"E komo mai&#8230; welcome in"},"content":{"rendered":"<blockquote><p><em>Onaona i ka hala me ka lehua<\/em>&#8230;<em>he hale lehua n\u014d ia na ka noe&#8230;\u02bbO ka\u02bbu n\u014d ia e \u02bbano\u02bbi nei, e li\u02bba nei ho\u02bbi o ka hiki mai&#8230;a hiki mai n\u014d \u02bboukou. A hiki p\u016b n\u014d me ke aloha&#8230; Aloha \u0113&#8230; aloha \u0113&#8230; aloha \u0113&#8230; <\/em><\/p>\n<p><em>-he mele aloha, <\/em>a chant used, in Hawai\u02bbi, to share aloha with others&#8230;<\/p><\/blockquote>\n<p>Welcome to WalkPono LLC! We are delighted to have you here.<\/p>\n<p>At WalkPono, we believe in the transformative power of mindfulness and forgiveness&#8230;especially when grounded in the powerful foundations of the <em>mo&#8217;omeheu Hawai&#8217;i<\/em>\u00a0and <i>nohona Hawai&#8217;i\u00a0<\/i>(Hawaiian culture).\u00a0Our mission is to accompany individuals and groups on a journey of self-discovery, healing, and personal growth.<\/p>\n<p>In today&#8217;s fast-paced world, finding moments of stillness and cultivating a compassionate mindset can be challenging. That&#8217;s why we are dedicated to providing you with the tools, techniques, and support needed to navigate life&#8217;s challenges with grace and resilience.<\/p>\n<p>Forgiveness is at the core of our work, as we recognize its profound impact on personal healing and liberation. Our forgiveness training programs provide a safe and nurturing space for you to explore the \u00a0power of forgiveness, both toward others and yourself. You&#8217;ll discover how forgiveness can release emotional burdens, foster inner peace, and open the door to deeper connections and personal growth.<\/p>\n<p>Whether you are seeking personal transformation, emotional healing, or a greater sense of self-awareness, WalkPono is here to support you every step of the way. Our experienced and compassionate team is dedicated to creating a warm and inclusive environment, where you can explore, learn, and grow.<\/p>\n<p>Thank you for visiting WalkPono.org. We look forward to accompanying you on your path to self-discovery and personal growth.&#8221;<\/p>\n","protected":false},"excerpt":{"rendered":"<p>Onaona i ka hala me ka lehua&#8230;he hale lehua n\u014d ia na ka noe&#8230;\u02bbO ka\u02bbu n\u014d ia e \u02bbano\u02bbi nei, e li\u02bba nei ho\u02bbi o ka hiki mai&#8230;a hiki mai n\u014d \u02bboukou. A hiki p\u016b n\u014d me ke aloha&#8230; Aloha \u0113&#8230; aloha \u0113&#8230; aloha \u0113&#8230; -he mele aloha, a chant used, in Hawai\u02bbi, to share &hellip; <\/p>\n<p class=\"link-more\"><a href=\"http:\/\/walkpono.org\/\" class=\"more-link\">Continue reading<span class=\"screen-reader-text\"> &#8220;E komo mai&#8230; welcome in&#8221;<\/span><\/a><\/p>\n","protected":false},"author":1,"featured_media":0,"parent":0,"menu_order":0,"comment_status":"closed","ping_status":"closed","template":"","meta":{"spay_email":""},"_links":{"self":[{"href":"http:\/\/walkpono.org\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/pages\/15"}],"collection":[{"href":"http:\/\/walkpono.org\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/pages"}],"about":[{"href":"http:\/\/walkpono.org\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/types\/page"}],"author":[{"embeddable":true,"href":"http:\/\/walkpono.org\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/users\/1"}],"replies":[{"embeddable":true,"href":"http:\/\/walkpono.org\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/comments?post=15"}],"version-history":[{"count":12,"href":"http:\/\/walkpono.org\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/pages\/15\/revisions"}],"predecessor-version":[{"id":351,"href":"http:\/\/walkpono.org\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/pages\/15\/revisions\/351"}],"wp:attachment":[{"href":"http:\/\/walkpono.org\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/media?parent=15"}],"curies":[{"name":"wp","href":"https:\/\/api.w.org\/{rel}","templated":true}]}}]